From: FingerBrowser
Subject: [PATCH 0014] skip canvas noise on small canvases

The readback noise (0010) perturbed every getImageData/toDataURL regardless
of canvas size. That tripped noise detectors: CreepJS getPixelMods writes
known data to an 8x8 canvas via putImageData and flags any difference on
getImageData, and putImageData->getImageData is lossless on a real browser.
Result was a "2% rgba noise" verdict.

Gate noise on the SOURCE CANVAS area (>= 1024 px), not the read region, so a
small sub-read of a large canvas is still noised and consistent with a full
read (preserving 0010's coordinate keying), while genuinely small canvases --
what these detectors probe -- stay lossless. Real fingerprinting reads
rendered text/gradients from canvases well above the threshold, so their
per-profile uniqueness is unaffected. Measured: CreepJS no longer reports rgba
noise; the fingerprint canvas hash stays unique.

Depends on: 0001-0013.

