+// Minimum canvas area (in pixels) to noise. Real fingerprinting reads rendered
+// content — text, gradients — from canvases well above this. Tiny canvases are
+// how noise detectors probe the readback path: CreepJS getPixelMods writes
+// known data to an 8x8 canvas via putImageData and flags any difference on
+// getImageData, and putImageData->getImageData is lossless on a real browser.
+// Gating on the SOURCE CANVAS size (not the read region) keeps that round-trip
+// lossless on small buffers while a small sub-read of a large canvas still gets
+// noised, preserving the coordinate consistency from the canvas-readback patch.
+inline constexpr int64_t kMinCanvasNoisePixels = 1024;
+
